                        "form": "буреве́стниках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "da25c315-14ce-3609-bb3c-34e1d40e93dd",
                        "entry_id": "b01d7396-457c-35ea-8854-f9262ae5bf1c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "зоол. птица отряда трубконосых"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b338cef9-d656-4106-b796-0217ec606885",
                                "sense_id": "da25c315-14ce-3609-bb3c-34e1d40e93dd",
                                "text": "Докучливо вьются чайки и буревестники над вспененным морем, провожая пароход; они словно радуются буре и с дикими криками носятся над волнами, играя с ними и перегоняя их..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f42609a6-d1dc-48fa-ba6c-9a8e175c3dfd",
                                "sense_id": "da25c315-14ce-3609-bb3c-34e1d40e93dd",
                                "text": "В этот момент моряки увидели над кораблём буревестников и чаек. Они реяли низко, а это служило признаком близости берегов."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "78a31274-5186-4e72-af64-6cb7a0b2f786",
                        "source_entry_id": "b01d7396-457c-35ea-8854-f9262ae5bf1c",
                        "source_sense_id": "da25c315-14ce-3609-bb3c-34e1d40e93dd",
                        "source_sense_description": "птица",
                        "target_lang_word": "petrel",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "petrel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0758704d-e814-3139-b536-f2fea181afbb",
                                        "entry_id": "e5e40532-e250-3132-ac0e-46177124071b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various species of black, grey, or white seabirds in the order Procellariiformes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15bd44ba-9f43-4717-8064-782b6a7829fa",
                                                "sense_id": "0758704d-e814-3139-b536-f2fea181afbb",
                                                "text": "The seventh of May following, we first saw many Birds in bignesse of Cliffe Pidgeons, and after divers other as Pettrels, Cootes, Hagbuts, Pengwins, Murres, Gannets, Cormorants, Guls, with many else in our English Tongue of no name."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83479d35-529e-410d-b23d-ef719454f65c",
                                                "sense_id": "0758704d-e814-3139-b536-f2fea181afbb",
                                                "text": "In a storm they will hover close under the ship's stern in the wake of the ship (as it is called) or the smoothness which the ship's passing has made on the sea; and there as they fly (gently then) they pat the water alternately with their feet as if they walked upon it; though still upon the wing. And from hence the seamen give them the name of petrels in allusion to St. Peter's walking upon the Lake of Gennesareth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf4e92aa-77f4-4ace-b18d-5cd56ac73ac4",
                        "source_entry_id": "b01d7396-457c-35ea-8854-f9262ae5bf1c",
                        "source_sense_id": "da25c315-14ce-3609-bb3c-34e1d40e93dd",
                        "source_sense_description": "птица",
                        "target_lang_word": "shearwater",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shearwater",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad19f3cb-ff83-333d-a36e-e4052d504a12",
                                        "entry_id": "20e32f2a-1096-3541-96a1-fd96a6d66bb3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the long-winged pelagic seabirds of the family Procellariidae in genera Puffinus, Ardenna, and Calonectris, that breed on islands and coastal cliffs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cea3d347-290d-4ea7-9e92-db9d299a4c15",
                                                "sense_id": "ad19f3cb-ff83-333d-a36e-e4052d504a12",
                                                "text": "At first I would not eat a frigate bird, a booby or a shearwater, but after a few months on the island I tried one broiled over coconut-shell coals, and I have never since missed an opportunity for such a feast."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65a9c1db-053b-3d52-96a4-4399663c3837",
                                        "entry_id": "20e32f2a-1096-3541-96a1-fd96a6d66bb3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the entire family Procellariidae, including certain of the petrels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
